s inherently dangerous. Use an adversarial buffer before passing retrieved chunks to the LLM.\n4.  **Adopt Optimistic Locking:** Prevent state corruption by ensuring no two agents can overwrite the `AgentState` without a version check.\n5.  **Graph Orchestration:** Migrate logic to a cyclic graph. This allows the system to natively handle \"loops\" (e.g., Reviewer returns to Coder) without custom, brittle `if/else` logic in `main.py`.\n\n**Analyst Note:** You are moving from a *scripted* multi-agent flow to an *orchestrated* one. By treating schemas as contracts and state as an atomic, versioned entity, you move from \"it works when the LLM behaves\" to \"it works because the system enforces the rules.\"", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "extra_content": {"google": {"thought_signature": "EjQKMgG+Pvb7NC5Ur5Hajyb8w/1lns0V2NBYZMF1m+eRxzqdXpWirxNEdS+AkVDEC4TvEzqu"}}}}], "created": 1774102908, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1122, "prompt_tokens": 6496, "total_tokens": 7618, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": null}}, "prompt_tokens": 6496, "completion_tokens": 1122, "agent_id": null}
